'''Frost dragons''' are a type of adult [[Dragon (race)|dragon]] located in the [[Grimstone Dungeon|dungeon]] on the island of [[Grimstone]], requiring 87 [[Sailing]] to access. A combat level of 85 is required to be assigned them as a slayer task, along with the Sailing requirement to access the island and completion of [[Dragon Slayer I]]. Once players have moored on the island at least once, it can also be accessed via [[fairy ring]] code {{Fairycode|DLP}}.

Like [[chromatic dragons]], frost dragons attack with melee and short-ranged [[dragonfire]]. However, they differ in several respects: their melee defences are weakest to crush, then stab, rather than stab alone; they have a 100% [[elemental weakness]] to fire spells rather than 50% to water spells; and while heavy ranged remains the best ranged option, they are more resistant to ranged attacks overall. As with all dragons, they are weak to [[dragonbane weapons]].  

Additionally, their dragonfire is considered [[Dragonfire#Icy breath|icy]], and will briefly freeze the player if they do not have adequate protection. This icy dragonfire can be partially negated by a regular [[antifire potion]], or fully negated using either a regular antifire potion with an [[anti-dragon shield]], or with a [[super antifire potion]] alone. Because they only use melee and short-ranged dragonfire, frost dragons can be [[Safespot|safespotted]].

They have the highest drop rate for [[dragon metal sheet]]s and [[dragon nails]] which is increased further when on a [[Slayer task]]. Loot from frost dragons spawns on their central north-eastern tile, as opposed to the south-westernmost tile for most monsters.

They do '''not''' count as blue dragons or metal dragons for [[Slayer task|Slayer tasks]] and instead have their own task. The odds of getting this task can be increased by 60% by purchasing the [[Slayer Rewards#Unlock|Chance of Heavy Frost]] unlock in the slayer rewards store. Also, the number of dragons assigned per task can be increased by purchasing the [[Slayer Rewards#Extend|I see Dragons]] unlock.

{{Bug|Attempting to attack frost dragons off-task in the task-only area currently displays a message from [[Nieve]] or [[Steve]] about sticking to your slayer task instead of the intended message.}}

